* {{hyphenation|en|days}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪz|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|daze}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|dayes}}, {{m|enm|dawes}}, from {{inh|en|ang|dagas}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*dagōs}}, {{m|gem-pro|*dagōz}}, plural of {{m|gem-pro|*dagaz}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|day|s|pos2=plural ending}}.

====Noun====
{{head|en|noun form}}

# {{plural of|en|day}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|p}}

# A particular time or period of vague extent.
#: {{ux|en|Things were more relaxed in Grandpa's '''days'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|His '''days''' of being the king are over.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=1|passage=In the old '''days''',&nbsp;[&hellip;], he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He never read me any of his manuscripts,&nbsp;[&hellip;], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned. But he had then none of the oddities and mannerisms which I hold to be inseparable from genius, and which struck my attention in after '''days''' when I came in contact with the Celebrity.}}
#* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=1|passage=He read the letter aloud. Sophia listened with the studied air of one for whom, even in these '''days''', a title possessed some surreptitious allurement.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1966
|author=w:David S. Nivison
|title=The Life and Thought of {{w|Chang Hsüeh-ch'eng}} (1738-1801)
|url=https://archive.org/details/lifethoughtofcha0000nivi/
|publisher=w:Stanford University Press
|LCCN=65-13112
|OCLC=906052523
